--- body ---
## Context

DOIfetch v0.3.0 was tagged on 2026-11-10: annotated, unsigned tag `v0.3.0` (tag object d76db1f)
on merge commit 95efea63e1ba2f4d7d6c8a6f9176cb8e691dd808 of MinhHaDuong/DOIfetch, following the
author ruling of 2026-10-29 on unsigned release tags. Filed from the DOIfetch interface session
that cut the release.

Since v0.2.0 the release carries:
- the default output directory is `docs` instead of `papers` (DOIfetch ticket 0029, requested
  from a harness session);
- HAL is looked up by DOI first and its download passes the bot check (DOIfetch ticket 0028);
- text files are LF, pinned by `.gitattributes` (DOIfetch ticket 0030).

The harness still pins v0.2.0 in two places that are meant to move together:
- `scripts/doifetch.sh`: `DOIFETCH_REF=v0.2.0`;
- `pyproject.toml`, dev group: `doifetch @ git+https://github.com/MinhHaDuong/DOIfetch@fc85d31…`
  with the comment "Keep in step with scripts/doifetch.sh v0.2.0, resolved commit".
`STATE.md` also names the pinned tag `v0.2.0`.

Not urgent: `scripts/doifetch.sh` already names its staging folder on every fetch, so the
changed default does not alter what the zotero skill does. The HAL fix is the part the harness
gains.

## Request

Move both pins to v0.3.0 (tag in `scripts/doifetch.sh`, resolved commit 95efea6… in
`pyproject.toml`, lock refreshed), and the tag named in `STATE.md`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `scripts/doifetch.sh` and the `pyproject.toml` dev dependency name v0.3.0 and its commit
- [ ] The tests that exercise the DOIfetch wrapper pass on the new pin
